Scope: final DI5 accessibility lane, frozen production behavior. DI5.1 F1 remains upheld historically and is corrected by attempt2. A new attempt2 focus-restoration regression blocks this verdict. This is not an invented acceptance verdict for the other lanes' full Go/race work, nor a full manual WCAG certification. No production, git, ledger, real data or deployment changes were made.

FAILURES

F2 — ACCESSIBILITY.md point 10, HTMX focus restoration; also relevant to point 9 keyboard continuity. web/static/js/page-refresh.js:32-49.
With the pending Page refresh notice's Keep editing button focused, an actual HTMX outerHTML replacement of main detaches and remounts the same notice. The same button and region survive, but document.activeElement becomes BODY, not the button or a sensible element inside the replaced region. Observed in light and dark, 390x900. The button is visibly present at x157.1875,y176,width120.578125,height42 after replacement, but no longer has keyboard focus. This is focus loss, not another overlay obstruction.

Independent real-render counterfactual command (cwd /tmp/DI5-2-a11y.6qv3pb):
  rtk proxy bash -lc 'set -o pipefail; node main-focus.cjs |& tee checker-evidence/main-focus.log'
Exit 1 at the explicit assertion: "constitution 10: restore focus after main swap". Four states completed before the assertion: previous script/light and dark retained the identical BUTTON; final script/light and dark returned BODY with sameButton=false, insideMain=false, buttonConnected=true, sameRegion=true, count=1.

The probe loads the actual isolated Dashboard handler/template render with all its scripts and real CSS. A GET-only intercepted /checker-main response uses the actual rendered main bytes; real htmx.ajax performs the outerHTML swap. Only the refresh API response is controlled to request the notice. This exercises the explicitly required main-replacement lifecycle; it does not claim that an ordinary Dashboard date request replaces main (that request updates KPIs and passes separately). The replacement response is a captured render, so this probe is NOT evidence about persistence of server-replaced input values. No server write or real app request occurs. The old/final counterfactual changes only the served page-refresh.js bytes, preserving the final Dashboard, CSS, scripts, viewport and swap.

Artifacts: checker-evidence/main-focus.json, main-focus.log, main-focus-{old,final}-{false,true}-{before,after}.png. The final light screenshot was inspected; the missing focus is established by activeElement/node identity, not by screenshot inference alone. Earlier corroboration used the worker's synthetic layout fixture with an independently added focused-notice state: focused-remount.cjs and checker-evidence/focused-remount/. That collector completed both themes; main-focus.cjs adds the explicit failing assertion and actual Dashboard render.

Attribution: this is introduced by attempt2 placing the notice inside main. Previous page-refresh.js SHA256 e4f515e7adcd11c4bad42d5ec1207a37809203e19899c25591d9574cb3e5aca8 leaves it outside the replaced main and retains focus. Current SHA256 97cb7c8c57d9bf9a885a8d0f86fea68a2a3d5f8377c071ed906997220c3e2ecf remounts it after focus has already fallen to BODY. The afterSwap handler reads document.activeElement too late to retain the detached button's focus. The scoped new code is:

@@ -29,6 +29,24 @@
+    function mountNotice() {
+        if (!notice || notice.isConnected) return;
+        var focus = document.activeElement;
+        var parent = document.querySelector('main') || document.body;
+        parent.insertBefore(notice, parent.firstChild);
+        // Insertion can push an editing control below the viewport. Keep that
+        // same control visible without moving keyboard focus to the notice.
+        if (focus && focus !== document.body && focus.isConnected) {
+            var rect = focus.getBoundingClientRect();
+            if (rect.top < 0 || rect.bottom > window.innerHeight ||
+                rect.left < 0 || rect.right > window.innerWidth) {
+                focus.scrollIntoView({block: 'nearest', inline: 'nearest', behavior: 'instant'});
+            }
+        }
+    }
+    // A main replacement can detach the pending region. Reuse its existing
+    // status and handlers; unrelated partial swaps must not repeat it.
+    document.addEventListener('htmx:afterSwap', mountNotice);

Full unified delta is checker-evidence/production.diff. Read-only `rtk proxy git -C /home/darrell/bin/ai/budget2/.worktrees/dashboard-insights diff master -- web/static/js/page-refresh.js` is empty because the file is not tracked in master; `git ... cat-file -e master:web/static/js/page-refresh.js` explicitly reports it absent. An empty tracked diff is not byte-identity proof. The immutable prior-script counterfactual above establishes the narrower attempt2 introduction directly. No claim that this issue existed at original69e484a.

